# IsaFlow

Next.js 14 + TypeScript multi-tenant accounting SaaS. Every DB query is scoped by `company_id`. Deployed to `app.isaflow.co.za`. Package manager: `bun@1.3.2`. Node `>=20.12.0`.

## Critical Rules

- Branch first: NEVER edit on `master`. First action is `git checkout -b <name>`.
- No stubs: build the real thing when CI fails on a missing module. No `return null` placeholders.
- Multi-tenant: ALWAYS add `company_id` to every DB query.
- DB: `sql` tagged template from `@/lib/neon` (legacy path; runtime is Supabase/pg). NEVER string-concat.
- API handlers: wrap with `withAuth(withErrorHandler(handler as any))` from `@/lib/auth`. Legacy `withCompany` is removed.
- Responses: `apiResponse.success/badRequest/notFound` from `@/lib/apiResponse`.
- Logging: `log` from `@/lib/logger`, never `console.log`.
- No empty `catch` blocks. 100% type coverage. Max 300 lines per file.
- pg returns `Date` objects from timestamp columns.
- Customer invoices: use `COALESCE(ci.client_id, ci.customer_id)`.
- Nav: update `src/components/accounting/accountingNavConfig.ts` for every new page.
- Migrations: next unused 3-digit prefix, `IF NOT EXISTS`, no prefix reuse.

## Commands

- `bun run dev` (port 3200), `bun run build`, `bun run lint`, `bun run type-check`, `bun run test:unit`, `bun run ci`, `bun run db:migrate`, `bash scripts/deploy.sh`.

## TDD enforced

Tests FIRST, implementation second. Vitest in `tests/unit/`, Playwright in `tests/e2e/`.

## Module docs

49 sibling `.claude.md` / `AGENTS.md` files give per-module rules under `src/modules/*` and `pages/api/accounting/*`.
